# evidence-review

Review semantic applicability, calibrate observations and investigate scoped tool evidence.

Use [guide.md](guide.md). Only controller-loaded references are available; links do not grant file access. Return the requested typed proposal; request missing source.

SEMANTIC REVERSE REVIEW Review actual materials, not just the generator's rationale. Separately examine (1) applicability of the obligation to the current API/configuration/fault contract; (2) necessity, sufficiency, alternatives and conditions of the obligation and support relation; (3) correspondence of the formal checker to the intended responsibility when a model is supplied. For each target cite the actual source IDs, explain the relevant expectation or dependency, seek contrary or weaker/stronger contracts, and state alternative mechanisms. Ask whether the obligation's bad outcome could still occur while the current obligations all hold. A successful model check does not answer that question. For checker correspondence inspect the actual predicate, trigger, context/identity comparisons, allowed initial states, excluded branches and observed events. Can the antecedent occur? Does the scope contain the relevant event? Do not claim nonvacuity or behavioral equivalence without an executed check; state missing evidence and request discriminating material or exploration. No issue found is a provisional scoped interpretation, not a proof or an independent consensus vote. A new invocation of the same backend can share the same mistakes. Do not strengthen or weaken a property solely to match the current code or a passing test.

SCOPED DISPOSITION AND REVISION Only revise existing objects explicitly listed in this review task. The controller computes the actual semantic write set, including binding associations and unit scope. Declare every changed field with exact JSON before and after values in changes. Fields that do not change must not be listed. Changing grounding or applicability does not require changing the claim text. Extra objects need a separate review; newly added candidates are not approved by this review. Classify the current judgment once: no_issue_found has no counterevidence; explained alternatives go in rationale, independent scope in limitations, and sourced challenges in disputed/revision_needed. For needs_reading, disputed or revision_needed, propose a finite reading/revision/investigation follow-up if supported. If none is legally actionable, explain the missing capability or material instead of inventing a request. Invocation completion does not resolve an issue. Resolve named issues against their prior evidence with resolves_issue_ids and attributed resolution_rationale. Use supersedes_task_ids only when this review fully covers the old versions, scope, materials and required aspects. A partial review cannot clear other issues. Harness-only changes do not resolve semantic disputes.

When resolution_issue_ids authorize reconsidering a prior model issue, compare prior_issue_models with the current model and its actual recheck. Resolve the stable issue against the corrected current model, without declaring the old model correct. A harness-only change or unrelated model cannot resolve a checker encoding dispute. A changed obligation meaning requires F2; unchanged meaning with a different encoding needs an attributed encoding_revision and correspondence review.

Return ReviewReply items for exactly required_review_pairs, citing attached source. In rationale assess applicability or necessity/sufficiency, alternatives and reverse consequences. Classify the current judgment explicitly: no_issue_found has no counterevidence; explained alternatives stay in rationale; independent scope and production exposure stay in limitations; a sourced challenge uses disputed/revision_needed with counterevidence; needs_reading identifies missing evidence and requests it when available. Missing aspects require focused follow-up and do not authorize approval or rewrites. Keep F2 revisions and issue resolutions attributed, and do not invent deployment choices. If this review also establishes stable reusable Behavior, Fact or Surface knowledge from attached source, optionally return one focused descriptive_delta under the existing AuditSpecDelta contract; never promote an observation, hypothesis or model assumption, duplicate existing knowledge, or use a descriptive delta to change a selected obligation.

